  nonce: f1eb  # f1eb
  message: "Closing as wont_do (audit 2026-04-26). WI-gudob umbrella claim covered Phases 1-5 (error_handler, controller, router, form, serializer concept linkers). Cohort findings: Phase 1 (error_handler) and Phase 5 (serializer) DO fire on airflow (3 + 17 hits) — those phases work for the FastAPI/Flask + DRF/Marshmallow targets airflow exercises. Phases 2-4 (controller/router/form) didn't fire for two distinct reasons: (a) cohort-001/iter-001 includes no decorator-based controller framework target (Spring, NestJS, Django, etc.); same root cause as WI-jolaf. (b) chatwoot IS a Rails app but rails.yaml never loaded — refine_frameworks demoted Rails to dev_frameworks because Ruby code lacks explicit import edges to the rails gem (Rails autoloads via Bundler/convention). The (b) finding is a separate structural bug filed as its own work item; addressing it would unblock validation of Rails-targeted phases via chatwoot. Net: this regression is a cohort-coverage gap plus the orthogonal Ruby-framework-demotion bug, not a code regression in the WI-gudob linkers themselves. To re-validate WI-gudob, the cohort needs (i) a decorator-based controller framework target for Phases 2-4 generally, and/or (ii) the Ruby-framework-demotion bug fixed so Rails apps actually exercise rails.yaml."  # f1eb
